</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PURPOSE - This rung continuously sends a 1-DINTmessage from the local 1756-L55 to a remote 1756-L55 over ControlNet.

SYSTEM CONFIGURATION - The local ControlLogix chassis consists of a 1756-L55 in slot 0 and a 1756-CNB (node 5) in slot 1.  The remote ControlLogix chassis also consists of a 1756-L55 in slot 0 and a 1756-CNB (node 6) in slot 1.  The two 1756-CNB modules are on the same ControlNet network.

THE MESSAGE INSTRUCTION - Under the 'Configuration' Tab in the message setup screen,  is selected as the message type, the Source Tag is created as a DINT called , the Destination Element is called , and the Number Of Elements is one.  Make sure that the Destination Element is a tag created in the remote controller with the same name and same data type.  These tags need to be created under the controller scope.  

Under the 'Communication' Tab in the Message setup screen, the path to the remote controller is specified.  The following describes the path (1, 1, 2, 6, 1, 0) used in this example:   indicates a connection to the backplane of the ControlLogix chassis,  indicates a connection to the CNB module in slot 1,  indicates a connection to port 2 of the CNB module (get on the  ControlNet wire),  indicates a connection to the remote CNB module at node address 6,  indicates a connection to the backplane of the remote ControlLogix chassis, and finally,  indicates a connection to the remote controller in slot 0.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(L55_to_L55.EN)MSG(L55_to_L55);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PURPOSE - This rung continuously reads data from location S:23 of a PLC5C at node 1.

SYSTEM CONFIGURATION - The ControlLogix chassis consists of a 1756-L55 in slot 0 and a 1756-CNB (node 5) in slot 1.   A PLC5C (node 1) is also on the same ControlNet network as the CNB module.

THE MESSAGE INSTRUCTION - Under the 'Configuration' Tab in the message setup screen,  is selected as the Message Type, the Source element is  of the PLC5C, the Destination Tag is named , and the Number Of Elements is one.  Make sure that the destination tag is created under the controller scope and has the same data type as the source tag (INT).

Under the 'Communication' Tab in the Message setup screen, the path to the PLC5C on ControlNet is specified.  The following describes the path (1, 1, 2, 7) used in this example:   indicates a connection to the backplane of the ControlLogix chassis,   indicates a connection to the CNB module in slot 1,   indicates a connection to port 2 of the CNB module (get on the ControlNet wire),   indicates a connection to the PLC5C at node address 7.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(L1_to_PLC5C.EN)MSG(L1_to_PLC5C);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
